{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The program does not condition on any top-level data variable with a sampling statement; `x0` is a context input used only to generate simulated quantities.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The model contains no parameters, no model-block likelihood, and no forbidden direct target manipulation. The generated-quantities RNG simulation is preserved unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  vector[3] x0;
}

transformed data {
  int<lower=0> M = 3;            // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N = 1000;         // Number of observations

  vector[M] z0 = [2, -2, 1]';
  real gamma0 = 10;               // True intercept
  vector[M] gamma1 = [2, -3, 1]'; // True slopes
  real nu = 2;                    // True Student degrees of freedom
  real sigma = 2;               // True measurement variability

}

generated quantities {
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix
  array[N] real y;      // Variates

  for (n in 1:N) {
    X[n, 1] = normal_rng(x0[1], 2);
    X[n, 2] = normal_rng(x0[2], 2);
    X[n, 3] = normal_rng(x0[3], 2);
    y[n] = student_t_rng(nu, gamma0 + (X[n] - z0') * gamma1, sigma);
  }
}

","data_safe_json":"{"x0":[4.562407242265079,3.9485622981738926,2.9854678018024945]}","protected_variables":[]}
